==English==
[[File:Chevy Express.JPG|thumb|right|A van (motor vehicle).]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|văn}}, {{IPA|en|/væn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-van.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Short for {{m-lite|en|caravan}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A covered [[motor vehicle]] used to carry [[goods]] or (normally less than ten) [[persons]], usually roughly [[cuboid]] in shape, longer and higher than a [[car]] but relatively smaller than a [[truck]]/[[lorry]] or a [[bus]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''van''' sped down the road.}}
#:{{syn|en|minivan|minibus|q1=chiefly if used to carry a few people; "minivan" is officially used in North America}}
# {{lb|en|British}} An enclosed railway vehicle for transport of goods, such as a [[boxcar]]/[[box van]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} A light [[wagon]], either covered or open, used by tradesmen and others for the [[transportation]] of [[goods]].
# {{lb|en|aerospace}} A large [[towable]] [[vehicle]] equipped for the [[repair]] of structures that cannot easily be moved.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1959|title=Western Aerospace|volume=39|page=46
|passage=Designed to be fully mobile and self-contained, the complete equipment includes an air-conditioned '''van''' containing all necessary electronic gear and a flat bed trailer in which missiles, jet engines and other large assemblies may be cleaned.}}

