* Forms beginning with {{m-lite|hu||v-}} are from {{der-lite|hu|fiu-pro|-}} {{m-lite|urj-pro|sc=Latinx|*wole-||to be}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|mns|sc=Cyrl|о̄луӈкве|tr=ōluňkve}}, {{cog-lite|fi|olla}} and {{cog-lite|et|olema}}. Compare inflected forms such as {{m-lite|hu|volt}}, {{m-lite|hu|volna}}, {{m-lite|hu|való}} and Old Hungarian {{m-lite|hu|vola}} or {{m-lite|hu|vala}}. The root in present tense (vagy-) is result of palatization: /vɒl/ > /vɒʎ/ > /vɒj/ > /vɒɟ/.

* Forms beginning with {{m-lite|hu||l-}} are from {{der-lite|hu|fiu-pro|-}} {{m-lite|urj-pro|sc=Latinx|*le-||to become}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|fi|lienee|pos=potential of {{m-lite|fi|olla}}}}, {{cog-lite|krl|lienöy|pos=potential of {{m-lite|krl|olla}}}}, {{cog-lite|se|leat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{audio|hu|Hu-van.ogg|Audio}}
